Sval: Picture-in-Picture ignores a hidden page whose tab is gone

With media.videocontrols.picture-in-picture.enable-when-switching-tabs.enabled
on, a page playing a video tells the parent when it goes hidden
(PictureInPicture:VideoTabHidden). A page made hidden as its tab closes,
as when an agent's Workspace is removed with a video playing in its
window, sends that message after the tab's browser has gone, and
PictureInPictureToggleParent read the missing browser and threw. No chrome
API reaches the actor's message handling.

diff --git a/toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/PictureInPicture.sys.mjs b/toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/PictureInPicture.sys.mjs
index 76ae77f16f..2a8f12c78d 100644
--- a/toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/PictureInPicture.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/PictureInPicture.sys.mjs
@@ -94,6 +94,11 @@ export class PictureInPictureToggleParent extends JSWindowActorParent {
         if (!lazy.PIP_ENABLED || !lazy.PIP_WHEN_SWITCHING_TABS) {
           break;
         }
+        // Sval: a page can go hidden as its tab closes, and then its message
+        // arrives once the tab's browser is gone.
+        if (!browser) {
+          break;
+        }
         // If the tab is still selected, then we can ignore this event
         if (browser.documentGlobal.gBrowser.selectedBrowser == browser) {
           break;
